IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wra-core`
IMPORT `wra4-ss96-97`

-- Tests for wra4-ss96-97.l4 (ss 96, 96A, 97). Every expected value is written from the text of the Act, beside the assertion.

§ `fixtures`

`s 96 test person P1` MEANS Person WITH `reference` IS "P1", `age in years` IS 40, `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1985, `where the person is` IS `England outside Greater London`, `where the person lives` IS `England outside Greater London`

GIVEN b IS A Benefit, amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN Award
`award of` MEANS Award WITH
    `the benefit awarded` IS b
    `who it is awarded to` IS `a single claimant` `s 96 test person P1`
    `the period awarded for` IS Period WITH `first day` IS Date 1 1 2025, `last day` IS Date 28 1 2025
    `the amount awarded for the period, in pounds` IS amount

`the awards of one household` MEANS LIST
    `award of` `universal credit` 1200,
    `award of` `personal independence payment` 500,
    `award of` `housing benefit` 300,
    `award of` `working tax credit` 200,
    `award of` `child benefit` 80

`a decision of kind` MEANS Decision WITH
    `the kind of decision` IS `a decision to apply the benefit cap`
    `the decision-maker` IS `the Secretary of State`
    `the benefit concerned` IS `universal credit`
    `the date it was made` IS Date 1 1 2025

GIVEN k IS A `Kind of decision`
GIVETH A Decision
`decision of kind` MEANS Decision WITH
    `the kind of decision` IS k
    `the decision-maker` IS `the Secretary of State`
    `the benefit concerned` IS `universal credit`
    `the date it was made` IS Date 1 1 2025

§ `s 96(10) "welfare benefit" means -- a closed list`

-- The list names (in its own order): bereavement allowance, child benefit, child tax credit, employment and support
-- allowance (including income-related), housing benefit, incapacity benefit, income support, jobseeker's allowance
-- (including income-based), maternity allowance, severe disablement allowance, universal credit, widow's pension,
-- widowed mother's allowance, widowed parent's allowance.
#ASSERT `s 96(10) the benefit is a welfare benefit` `bereavement allowance` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 96(10) the benefit is a welfare benefit` `child benefit` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 96(10) the benefit is a welfare benefit` `child tax credit` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 96(10) the benefit is a welfare benefit` `contributory employment and support allowance` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 96(10) the benefit is a welfare benefit` `income-related employment and support allowance` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 96(10) the benefit is a welfare benefit` `housing benefit` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 96(10) the benefit is a welfare benefit` `incapacity benefit` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 96(10) the benefit is a welfare benefit` `income support` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 96(10) the benefit is a welfare benefit` `contribution-based jobseeker's allowance` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 96(10) the benefit is a welfare benefit` `income-based jobseeker's allowance` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 96(10) the benefit is a welfare benefit` `maternity allowance` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 96(10) the benefit is a welfare benefit` `severe disablement allowance` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 96(10) the benefit is a welfare benefit` `universal credit` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 96(10) the benefit is a welfare benefit` `widow's pension` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 96(10) the benefit is a welfare benefit` `widowed mother's allowance` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 96(10) the benefit is a welfare benefit` `widowed parent's allowance` EQUALS TRUE
-- Not on the list, so not a welfare benefit (the definition says "means"): working tax credit (only child tax credit is named),
-- council tax benefit, state pension credit, housing credit, personal independence payment, disability living allowance,
-- industrial injuries benefit, social fund payment, guardian's allowance.
#ASSERT `s 96(10) the benefit is a welfare benefit` `working tax credit` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 96(10) the benefit is a welfare benefit` `council tax benefit` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 96(10) the benefit is a welfare benefit` `state pension credit` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 96(10) the benefit is a welfare benefit` `housing credit` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 96(10) the benefit is a welfare benefit` `personal independence payment` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 96(10) the benefit is a welfare benefit` `disability living allowance` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 96(10) the benefit is a welfare benefit` `industrial injuries benefit` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 96(10) the benefit is a welfare benefit` `social fund payment` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 96(10) the benefit is a welfare benefit` `guardian's allowance` EQUALS FALSE

§ `s 96(10) couple, single person, regulations, prescribed`

-- "couple" means two persons of a prescribed description.
#ASSERT `s 96(10) the two persons are a couple` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 96(10) the two persons are a couple` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 96(10) the two persons are a couple` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- "single person" means a person who is not a member of a couple.
#ASSERT `s 96(10) the person is a single person` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 96(10) the person is a single person` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 96(10) the person is a single person` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- "regulations" means regulations made by the Secretary of State.
#ASSERT `s 96(10) regulations made by this maker are regulations` `the Secretary of State` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 96(10) regulations made by this maker are regulations` `an authorised person` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 96(10) regulations made by this maker are regulations` `an employment officer` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 96(10) regulations made by this maker are regulations` `Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 96(10) regulations made by this maker are regulations` `a local authority` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 96(10) regulations made by this maker are regulations` `the First-tier Tribunal` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 96(10) regulations made by this maker are regulations` `the Upper Tribunal` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 96(10) regulations made by this maker are regulations` `a court` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 96(10) regulations made by this maker are regulations` `the Director of Public Prosecutions` EQUALS FALSE
-- "prescribed" means prescribed in regulations.
#ASSERT `s 96(10) the matter is prescribed` TRUE `the Secretary of State` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 96(10) the matter is prescribed` TRUE `a local authority` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 96(10) the matter is prescribed` FALSE `the Secretary of State` EQUALS FALSE

§ `s 96(5A) the annual limit, and s 96(5B)(c) the relevant amount`

-- (a) £25,323 or £16,967, for persons resident in Greater London; (b) £22,020 or £14,753, for other persons.
#ASSERT `s 96(5A) the annual limit` (JUST TRUE) (JUST `s 96(5A) the first figure`) EQUALS JUST 25323
#ASSERT `s 96(5A) the annual limit` (JUST TRUE) (JUST `s 96(5A) the second figure`) EQUALS JUST 16967
#ASSERT `s 96(5A) the annual limit` (JUST FALSE) (JUST `s 96(5A) the first figure`) EQUALS JUST 22020
#ASSERT `s 96(5A) the annual limit` (JUST FALSE) (JUST `s 96(5A) the second figure`) EQUALS JUST 14753
-- "resident" is defined by regulations (s 96(5B)(b)), and which figure applies is for regulations (s 96(5B)(a)): not covered.
#ASSERT `s 96(5A) the annual limit` NOTHING (JUST `s 96(5A) the first figure`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 96(5A) the annual limit` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 96(5A) the annual limit` (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

-- Dividing an annual limit by 12 reference periods: 22,020 / 12 = 1,835 exactly; 25,323 / 12 = 2,110.25.
#ASSERT `s 96(5B)(c) the annual limit divided into reference periods` 22020 12 (JUST (`s 96(5B)(c) rounded up to a multiple of` OF 1)) EQUALS JUST 1835
#ASSERT `s 96(5B)(c) the annual limit divided into reference periods` 22020 12 (JUST (`s 96(5B)(c) rounded down to a multiple of` OF 1)) EQUALS JUST 1835
#ASSERT `s 96(5B)(c) the annual limit divided into reference periods` 25323 12 (JUST (`s 96(5B)(c) rounded up to a multiple of` OF 1)) EQUALS JUST 2111
#ASSERT `s 96(5B)(c) the annual limit divided into reference periods` 25323 12 (JUST (`s 96(5B)(c) rounded down to a multiple of` OF 1)) EQUALS JUST 2110
#ASSERT `s 96(5B)(c) the annual limit divided into reference periods` 25323 12 (JUST (`s 96(5B)(c) rounded down to a multiple of` OF 0.01)) EQUALS JUST 2110.25
#ASSERT `s 96(5B)(c) the annual limit divided into reference periods` 25323 12 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 96(5B)(c) the annual limit divided into reference periods` 25323 0 (JUST (`s 96(5B)(c) rounded down to a multiple of` OF 1)) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 96(3) the reference period`

-- A reference period of a prescribed duration, here 28 days from 1 January 2025: both ends count, so it ends on 28 January 2025.
#ASSERT (`s 96(3) the reference period` (Date 1 1 2025) (JUST 28)) EQUALS JUST (Period WITH `first day` IS Date 1 1 2025, `last day` IS Date 28 1 2025)
#ASSERT (`s 96(3) the reference period` (Date 1 1 2025) (JUST 1)) EQUALS JUST (Period WITH `first day` IS Date 1 1 2025, `last day` IS Date 1 1 2025)
#ASSERT (`s 96(3) the reference period` (Date 1 1 2025) NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 96(3) the reference period` (Date 1 1 2025) (JUST 0)) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 96(2) the cap`

-- Only welfare benefits count: 1200 universal credit + 300 housing benefit + 80 child benefit = 1580; personal independence
-- payment and working tax credit are not on the s 96(10) list.
#ASSERT `s 96(2) the total entitlement to welfare benefits` `the awards of one household` EQUALS 1580
#ASSERT `s 96(2) the total entitlement to welfare benefits` EMPTY EQUALS 0
-- "exceeds" is strict: equal to the relevant amount is not an excess; one penny more is.
#ASSERT `s 96(2) the total entitlement exceeds the relevant amount` 2110.25 2110.25 EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 96(2) the total entitlement exceeds the relevant amount` 2110.26 2110.25 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 96(2) the total entitlement exceeds the relevant amount` 2110.24 2110.25 EQUALS FALSE
-- The reduction is "up to or equalling the excess": the excess is the most.
#ASSERT `s 96(2) the greatest reduction the cap can require` 2500 (JUST 2110.25) EQUALS JUST 389.75
#ASSERT `s 96(2) the greatest reduction the cap can require` 2110.26 (JUST 2110.25) EQUALS JUST 0.01
#ASSERT `s 96(2) the greatest reduction the cap can require` 2110.25 (JUST 2110.25) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 96(2) the greatest reduction the cap can require` 1000 (JUST 2110.25) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 96(2) the greatest reduction the cap can require` 2500 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 96(1) and s 96(4)(c) whether a cap is applied`

#ASSERT `s 96(1) a benefit cap is applied to the person's welfare benefits` NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 96(1) a benefit cap is applied to the person's welfare benefits` (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 96(1) a benefit cap is applied to the person's welfare benefits` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 96(1) a benefit cap is applied to the person's welfare benefits` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 96(1) a benefit cap is applied to the person's welfare benefits` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE

§ `s 96(9) devolved benefits`

#ASSERT `s 96(9) benefit cap regulations may reduce this welfare benefit` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 96(9) benefit cap regulations may reduce this welfare benefit` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 96(9) benefit cap regulations may reduce this welfare benefit` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 96(9) benefit cap regulations may reduce this welfare benefit` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 96A the five-year review`

-- Last review on 15 June 2020: the next is due by 15 June 2025 (five years on); the day after is overdue.
#ASSERT `s 96A(1) the latest day for the next review of the sums` (Date 15 6 2020) EQUALS Date 15 6 2025
#ASSERT `s 96A(1) the five-year review is overdue` (Date 15 6 2020) (Date 14 6 2025) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 96A(1) the five-year review is overdue` (Date 15 6 2020) (Date 15 6 2025) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 96A(1) the five-year review is overdue` (Date 15 6 2020) (Date 16 6 2025) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 96A(2) the Secretary of State may review the sums at this time` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 96A(2) the Secretary of State may review the sums at this time` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 96A(3) the review met the requirement to take account of the national economic situation` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 96A(3) the review met the requirement to take account of the national economic situation` FALSE EQUALS FALSE

§ `s 97(6) no appeal against a decision to apply the benefit cap`

#ASSERT `s 97(6) SSA1998 Sch 2 para 8A an appeal lies against the decision` (`decision of kind` `a decision to apply the benefit cap`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 97(6) SSA1998 Sch 2 para 8A an appeal lies against the decision` (`decision of kind` `a decision on entitlement to a benefit or on its amount`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 97(6) SSA1998 Sch 2 para 8A an appeal lies against the decision` (`decision of kind` `a decision on limited capability for work or work-related activity`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 97(6) SSA1998 Sch 2 para 8A an appeal lies against the decision` (`decision of kind` `a decision on ability to carry out daily living or mobility activities`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 97(6) SSA1998 Sch 2 para 8A an appeal lies against the decision` (`decision of kind` `a decision that an amount is recoverable or on how much`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 97(6) SSA1998 Sch 2 para 8A an appeal lies against the decision` (`decision of kind` `a decision on the amount payable after loss of benefit for an offence`) EQUALS NOTHING
